				"subject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> defines the identity, facial features, black hair, gray-blue eyes, school uniform, black backpack, and colors of the male student. <Picture 2> defines the identity, facial features, pale blond twin-tail hair with pink lower strands, pink eyes, hairpins, school clothing, black backpack, and colors of Yuzaki Shino. <Picture 3> defines the residential street, concrete drainage channel, tiled wall, metal guardrail, houses, vegetation, late-afternoon light, and environmental colors. <Picture 4> defines the male student's question, Yuzaki Shino's initial reaction, framing, and character placement while excluding all printed elements. <Picture 5> defines her answer, follow-up expression, framing, and shot order while excluding all printed elements. <Subject 1> is the male student, linked to speaker (S1), with the fixed voice anchor: male teenager, medium-low pitch, quiet restrained voice. <Subject 2> is Yuzaki Shino, linked to speaker (S2), with the fixed voice anchor: female teenager, medium-high pitch, bright expressive voice.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] An independent six-second question-and-answer beside the drainage channel: the male student asks when work starts, and Yuzaki Shino answers that it starts at five.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1>: attribute_transfer for <Subject 1>'s identity, face, hair, uniform, backpack, and colors in every shot.\n<Picture 2>: attribute_transfer for <Subject 2>'s identity, face, hair, hairpins, clothing, backpack, and colors in every shot; dirt remains as a temporary story-state attribute.\n<Picture 3>: attribute_transfer for the street, drainage channel, wall, rail, houses, vegetation, light, and environmental colors in every shot.\n<Picture 4>: partially_preserved for the work-time question, listening positions, and initial surprised reaction in Shot 1 and Shot 2; exclude borders, bubbles, titles, captions, sound-effect marks, and every readable or text-like element.\n<Picture 5>: partially_preserved for Yuzaki Shino's time answer and questioning look in Shot 3; exclude borders, bubbles, captions, sound-effect marks, and every readable or text-like element.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is in full color. Male appearance follows <Picture 1>; Yuzaki Shino's appearance follows <Picture 2>; the residential drainage environment follows <Picture 3>; the question beat follows <Picture 4>; the answer beat and final framing follow <Picture 5>. No panel borders, speech bubbles, captions, subtitles, watermarks, logos, UI, or readable text appear.\n[Shot 1] A compact independent two-shot establishes <Subject 1> and dirty, flustered <Subject 2> facing each other beside the drainage channel. <Subject 1> (S1) asks with sudden practical concern: <d>[Chinese] 打工？几点开始？</d> Only his lips move.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, <Subject 2> blinks, tilts her head toward him, and (S2) answers with brief confusion followed by a quick explanation: <d>[Chinese] 欸？……五点开始，怎么了？</d> <Subject 1> closes his mouth and listens; the question-and-answer closes completely.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft residential ambience, distant birds, light clothing movement, and natural breaths between the rapid speaker changes.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n\n[Prohibited items]\n\nText / subtitles / UI / watermarks / logos / corner badges / letters / numbers / symbols / glyphs / pseudo-text / text-like graphic shapes / comic speech bubbles / comic sound-effect marks / real-world UI\n\n[Mandatory declaration]\n\nClean full-screen animation footage, not a comic page or UI. No background music; keep only ambient sound, human voices, and sound effects. Do not render any subtitles, text, letters, numbers, symbols, glyphs, pseudo-text, watermarks, logos, speech bubbles, or sound-effect marks. Spoken dialogue inside <d> is audio only and must never appear visually.",
